# Android App

The Artemis Android application allows you to manage PFS archives on the go. It uses Go compiled as a shared library via JNI.

## Prerequisites

- **Android SDK**: compileSdk 35
- **Android NDK**: r29+
- **Go**: 1.26+

## Build Instructions

1. **Cross-compile Go shared library**:

```bash
./build-android.sh
```

2. **Build the APK**:

```bash
cd android
./gradlew assembleDebug
```

The APK will be generated at `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`.

> **Note:** If you are working in a non-Termux environment, please remove `android.aapt2FromMavenOverride=/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/opt/android-sdk/build-tools/35.0.0/aapt2` from your Gradle configuration.
